  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_402e587489f44904990d7b2fe1c62077",
      "statement": "The evaluation subsystem ships exactly one console entry, `manifold-eval` (registered as `manifold.eval.cli:main`), while `manifold.eval` is the library surface exporting `BeforeAfterEval`, `BeforeAfterResult`, `SliceGrid`, `ComparisonPageBuilder`, `JitComparison`, and `ControlNetComparison`; the report builder deliberately has no console script of its own.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L80-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17bcac43bbb0d405acdd522f3591668602f0db4ab529176961deff526288d3c3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/__init__.py#L14-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c03d7831ead77e3ca100447ead2ee8370cbd2fb5a62f0ee331539640fa989ba2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1505399d33114ce8bf348dc44375bce3",
      "statement": "The evaluation policy is dispatched from the before artifact's own `model_index.json` (`pipeline_class`) with no mode flag: `LatentFlowPipeline` routes to the unconditional pass, `ControlNetLatentFlowPipeline` to the paired pass, a missing index raises `FileNotFoundError`, and an unknown class raises a `ValueError` naming the supported classes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L132-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dff360e6a172ed549e51f000b8f245d179bcd3d36ec24864623bfe719ecde6a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e25ce687a4b944fa9eb4d5ab909da206",
      "statement": "The CLI builds the after policy by loading a probe pipeline from the before export, running the ADR-0006 `export_to_native` bridge to write `<output>/after_native`, and then reloading both native directories into fresh pipelines, so the bridge's in-place bake of the probe components cannot contaminate the before side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L260-L286",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac613e21755943574961a7e095cec32c8170099bef7943ba8da3225dfee4856b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/export.py#L83-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f3f205f57160447da7d452f4d06638b1e798bc798a6319efa3c0c635a9c749a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f9f8a7f62f714971bcaed0499ee18b1d",
      "statement": "A ControlNet after export passes the frozen base UNet through verbatim and bakes only the checkpoint's `controlnet.*` weights; a checkpoint that carries no `controlnet.*` keys is rejected with a `ValueError` rather than silently exported.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L269-L279",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be255db8e05bfaad5cb71fc80e18b35e875dca102ab3a82e2a6d2114b23780fc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/export.py#L83-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dc4a7aa9c7e53f319688b7296f674b9c5cf8e80e1e672a2200e5452fbc83a6a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fb7521a8229e40ab9a3e4df62dc9c77e",
      "statement": "The same-noise fairness contract is enforced inside the driver: the unconditional pass hands each side a fresh `torch.Generator` seeded with the same seed on the pipeline device, and the paired pass draws one noise tensor and passes that same tensor to both `sample_latent` calls.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L125-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8955b042f36e9159487ed6372721602d0fb66aa47329787f4cdc9e1217feed4d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L187-L199",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6e2a11e8fe719fb56eff18a167f0ba812796cebec60646b9dfe1306b6672704:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c2cc102898c14f46bf1615a1e48d7b1d",
      "statement": "Every volume the eval compares or renders (before, after, and the real target) is decoded in float32 through the frozen VAE via `LatentDecoder` and then per-volume min-max normalized to `[0,1]` by the shared `min_max_to_unit`, which maps a degenerate zero-range volume to zeros; that shared convention is what lets the fidelity metric assume `data_range = 1.0`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L82-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:321a8fdec1fc36142709a26b0755561321573b61e005bbc81a77b60d56696667:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/pipelines/pipeline_utils.py#L26-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd122d6dc1889d50fab432e7bf7aaee3d34496e86896526cef80d6f922291a9e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7fe9622c22cd404bbdc097515c05993c",
      "statement": "`PairedFidelityMetrics` composes MONAI `PSNRMetric(max_val=1.0)` and `SSIMMetric(spatial_dims=3, data_range=1.0)` over equal `[B,C,D,H,W]` tensors already normalized to `[0,1]`, raises a `ValueError` on a shape mismatch before MONAI sees the pair, and batch-means both outputs; PSNR is `+inf` for identical volumes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired.py#L34-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63ba2b62f6a540d4a824f5d4e19571e2699658897e9a0f2bacac56064883a963:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_003a4613511843a787ef4c22385fe7cb",
      "statement": "The eval artifacts are one 2.5D three-plane slice-grid PNG per sample plus a `metrics.json` recording the policy, seed, inference-step count, sample count, and grid basenames (plus before/after PSNR and SSIM for the paired policy); grid references are recorded as basenames so the report stays portable after the eval directory is moved.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L147-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74d37cac36a28716d4ca89e744e3e54aee9fb800351e417c781c4ac8ec1cdd2c:"
